&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Principal Infrastructure Security Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location: Dublin, IE&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ridgeline is hiring a Principal Infrastructure Security Engineer to set the direction for cloud and infrastructure security across every product line, account, and environment. You will define the architecture vision and the security invariants that guide engineering decisions, and you will be accountable for Ridgeline’s overall cloud security posture.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work with Engineering, Product Management, and Technology leaders on cloud security trade-offs that carry business, regulatory, or reputational consequences. You will also help build the team&#39;s technical culture and develop Staff-level engineers, so that its standards, detection frameworks, and architectural judgment last beyond any single project. We believe in a culture where security is everyone&#39;s responsibility and an integral part of our engineering philosophy.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Ridgeline, how we work matters as much as what we build. Ridgeliners act like owners, choose growth over comfort, and communicate with transparency. We assume positive intent, bias toward action, and bring solutions—not just problems. We celebrate wins, learn from setbacks, and thrive in a resilient, collaborative, high-performing culture.&lt;br&gt;If this excites you, we’d love to meet you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You must be permitted to work in Ireland, including under EU work authorization, without the need for employer sponsorship.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the multi-year cloud security architecture vision and the security invariants that govern engineering decisions across all product lines, AWS accounts, and infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set the technical strategy for cloud security tooling and automation, including how AI changes security operations, and make the build-versus-buy decisions that determine what the team can do for years.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive company-wide guardrails and controls in our AWS environment (e.g., SCPs, IAM boundaries, AWS managed security services, custom-built solutions, and policy-as-code), and implement the standards and processes that keep them enforced.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop threat models and security approaches, and identify emerging threats to identity, data, AI workloads, and infrastructure before they become problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create frameworks and methodologies for securely integrating third-party cloud services and internal platforms, and see them adopted across Ridgeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate broad changes in cloud and infrastructure security, identify where our current approach stops scaling, and propose fixes before it does.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build AI and automation frameworks, and partner across functions to deploy reusable agents that multiple teams use.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver large, cross-team projects on schedule and at high quality, breaking complex programs into pieces the contributing teams can execute.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the cloud security team&#39;s long-term technical culture, develop Staff-level cloud security engineers, and sponsor the next leaders at Ridgeline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape C-suite and board-level decisions on cloud security investment, cloud adoption strategy, and organizational risk acceptance.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are &amp;amp; What Makes You Qualified:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of relevant experience in cloud security or platform engineering, including experience leading large cross-team initiatives with company-wide impact and delivering them on schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in at least one high-level language (Python strongly preferred; Kotlin or TypeScript a plus).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level experience with AWS, especially in the following areas:&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identity and Access Management (IAM, Orgs &amp;amp; SCPs, Identity Center)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Networking (VPC, Security Groups, Transit Gateway, Load Balancers, Network Firewall)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compute (EKS, ECS, Lambda)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data Persistence (S3, Aurora, DynamoDB)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Logging &amp;amp; Monitoring (GuardDuty, CloudTrail, CloudWatch)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success defining enterprise-wide access management strategy and policy frameworks (IAM/SCPs), and cloud security architecture that engineering teams adopted.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of cloud workload protection, infrastructure monitoring, and threat detection in AWS-native environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert-level experience securing Kubernetes and Amazon EKS (including EKS Auto Mode): cluster access control, network policy, Istio service mesh, Kyverno admission policy, and image signing with cosign.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency with infrastructure-as-code (e.g., OpenTofu or Terraform), GitOps delivery (e.g., ArgoCD), and CI/CD practices, and experience setting tooling and automation strategy, including build-versus-buy decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to present cloud security risk and trade-offs to executives, and to influence investment, cloud adoption, and risk acceptance decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of anticipating broad change in cloud security and acting on it before it became urgent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building AI or automation frameworks and reusable agents that change how cross-functional teams work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing senior engineers and sponsoring emerging leaders, and building team standards, detection frameworks, and architectural judgment that outlast individual projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Scopely&lt;/strong&gt; is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Identity Security Engineer &lt;/strong&gt;to join our Information Security team on a remote basis or hybrid basis if located in Barcelona.&amp;nbsp; This is a hands-on engineer who will build identity controls that reduce excessive privilege and protect critical operations. You will improve access across employee, player, business partner, and non-human identities by building AI-native identity workflows: agentic systems that handle provisioning, access reviews, and remediation within explicit guardrails, with humans approving what matters. Your work will protect the identities and access that support Scopely’s critical business processes, including essential enterprise functions and game operations.&amp;nbsp; This is a highly technical, hands-on role for someone who can operate across AWS, GCP, Okta, AWS IAM Identity Center, Zero Trust access models, identity governance workflows, and modern AI-enabled engineering environments, while building scalable identity systems through Infrastructure as Code, workflow orchestration, and automation-first security engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reduce identity attack surface and privilege&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduce standing and excessive access with least-privilege roles, just-in-time and time-bound elevation, and automated access reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build repeatable identity and access workflows that make onboarding, approvals, role changes, reviews, and offboarding consistent, traceable, and timely.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Govern non-human identities, including service accounts, workload identities, CI/CD identities, API credentials, and AI agents and their tool integrations: inventory them, assign owners, replace long-lived secrets with short-lived or federated credentials, and rotate or revoke on a schedule and on signal.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengthen identity protection and resilience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Protect access to critical business processes and systems with phishing-resistant authentication (passkeys/FIDO2), device trust and posture signals, tightly controlled privileged access, and prompt revocation of suspicious sessions or compromised credentials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Threat-model identity platforms, integrations, and access paths to identify exploitable trust relationships, privilege escalation, and credential misuse.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build identity telemetry and response workflows to detect risky sign-ins, privilege changes, credential misuse, and compromised integrations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and test break-glass and recovery procedures for identity services and cloud access so teams can regain secure access during an outage or compromise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extend the same patterns to player and partner identities where security owns the controls: platform identity federation (Apple, Google, Steam, console), account linking and recovery, external and vendor access, and defenses against account takeover and credential stuffing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build AI-native identity services&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and operate reusable identity controls and services using infrastructure as code, APIs, scripting, and delivery pipelines. Apply code review, testing, drift detection, and audit trails so that every change, whether made by an engineer or an agent, is safe to deploy and easy to investigate.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build multi-agent workflows that surface identity risk, run access attestations, and triage and remediate access issues end to end. Engineer the harness those agents run in: scoped tools and permissions, curated context and data access, evals and test cases, orchestration between agents, and observability, so agent behavior is predictable, reviewable, and improvable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Treat agents as identities. Give every agent and MCP integration its own scoped credentials, least-privilege permissions, and bounded data access; validate inputs and outputs; log every action; and require human approval for changes that touch privileged access or production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with game and platform stakeholders to adopt shared identity patterns. Measure progress through reduced standing privilege, stale access, and unmanaged identities, and less manual work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce audit-ready evidence for access reviews, privileged access, and lifecycle events as a byproduct of the workflows rather than a separate project.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in IAM, or identity-focused cloud/security engineering, including hands-on ownership of production identity controls in complex environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with Okta or a comparable workforce identity platform and AWS/GCP IAM, as well as federation and provisioning protocols such as SAML, OIDC, OAuth, and SCIM.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production experience building, testing, and operating identity services or automation using Terraform or comparable infrastructure as code, Python, Go, or TypeScript., APIs, version control, and CI/CD.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong knowledge of least privilege, just-in-time privileged access, identity lifecycle and governance, authentication controls, and non-human or workload identity risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience threat-modeling identity architectures, integrations, and access paths, and driving remediation with service owners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building AI-native workflows: systems where agents carry out multi-step work end to end, designed from the start around what agents can be trusted to do and where humans approve. Using a coding a

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://fin.ai/&quot;&gt;Fin&lt;/a&gt;, now part of Salesforce, is on a mission to help businesses provide perfect customer experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our AI Agent Fin is the highest-performing AI Customer Agent on the market today, enabling businesses to deliver impeccable, always-on customer support across the customer journey, from service, to sales, to ecommerce. Powered by our own AI models, Fin resolves complex customer issues end-to-end across every channel, with minimal set-up and integration. Fin can also be combined with our natively integrated Intercom help desk, giving modern support teams one single system.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Together with Salesforce, the #1 AI CRM, where humans with agents drive customer success, we&#39;re building the future of customer experience. Here, ambition meets action. Tech meets trust. And innovation isn&#39;t a buzzword, it&#39;s a way of life. The world of work as we know it is changing, and we&#39;re looking for Trailblazers who are passionate about bettering business and the world through AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ready to level up your career at the company leading workforce transformation in the agentic era? You&#39;re in the right place. Agentforce is the future of AI, and you are the future of Salesforce.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fin is the AI Customer Service company on a mission to help businesses provide incredible customer experiences.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our AI agent Fin, the most advanced customer service AI agent on the market, lets businesses deliver always-on, impeccable customer service and ultimately transform their customer experiences for the better. Fin can also be combined with our Helpdesk to become a complete solution called the Fin Customer Service Suite, which provides AI enhanced support for the more complex or high touch queries that require a human agent.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2011 and trusted by over 30,000 global businesses, Fin is setting the new standard for customer service. Driven by our core values, we push boundaries, build with speed and intensity, and consistently deliver incredible value to our customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s the opportunity?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re hiring an &lt;strong&gt;Engineering Manager&lt;/strong&gt; for our &lt;strong&gt;AI Models Infrastructure Team&lt;/strong&gt; in the &lt;strong&gt;AI Group&lt;/strong&gt;. The AI Models Infrastructure team builds and operates the foundational infrastructure that empowers our teams to train and run Fin&#39;s own AI models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a &lt;strong&gt;highly technical EM role&lt;/strong&gt; - you’ll lead a team of expert engineers in a fast-evolving technical domain. In order to empower this team to be most effective, you will need prior experience in AI, and the appetite to continually invest in deepening your technical knowledge.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Learn more about Fin&#39;s engineering culture at&lt;a href=&quot;https://intercom.engineering&quot;&gt; intercom.engineering&lt;/a&gt;, and more about Fin at &lt;a href=&quot;http://fin.ai&quot;&gt;fin.ai&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What will I be doing?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead a high-performing team&lt;/strong&gt; building the platform and infrastructure that power Fin&#39;s AI capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Magnify the team’s effectiveness&lt;/strong&gt;, whether that means removing impediments, or finding ways to accelerate their progress.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support teams of ML Scientists and Engineers &lt;/strong&gt;building AI powered capabilities&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Plan, prioritize, and deliver&lt;/strong&gt; high-impact roadmaps in partnership with the team’s most senior engineers, balancing delivery, quality, and innovation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Empower the engineers on the team to act with agency and maximize their impact.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expand your scope over time&lt;/strong&gt;, potentially taking ownership of additional platform domains as the team and AI initiatives grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What skills do I need?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You must have:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading infra or platform teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong prior experience working as an engineer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong technical judgment and communication skills, enabling you to advocate for the team’s needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Adaptable leadership style suited to a group that will grow quickly, and change shape over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity and enthusiasm for AI.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience training ML models and operating them in production at scale is a significant advantage, but not a hard requirement. We will invest in EMs with a deep technical background, and a strong appetite to learn the domain.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience training ML models and operating them in production, at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
